    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24807_p11_b49",
      "text": "Table 5 shows strong gains on COCO and ADE20K, despite our method using\nno unlabelled data while several baselines rely on large semi-supervised training\nsets (SemiVL [12], UniMatchV2 [37]). Compared to the labelled-only variant of\nUniMatchV2, our results highlight the effectiveness of prompt-conditioned seg-\nmentation even without additional data. Importantly, these improvements are\nnot explained by backbone capacity alone: a CLIP+SAM baseline with simi-\nlar backbones but without semantic adapters performs substantially worse (see\nExperiment 2 and Table 3).\n",
      "bbox": [
        134.76,
        390.93,
        480.61,
        484.57
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        539,
        1563,
        1922,
        1938
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "SFRM1000",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 564,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24807_p11_b50",
      "text": "Performance differences are smaller on PASCAL VOC, a simpler dataset\nwhere prompt-based conditioning offers less advantage and factors such as back-\nbone capacity and semi-supervised training become more influential.\n",
      "bbox": [
        134.76,
        486.57,
        480.58,
        520.44
      ],
